if I were president, I'd implement "single payer foodcare"
this is where the government steps in at the distributor layer and pays for food
all of it
and the downstream can take as much as they need.

this rewards small farmers, who simply have to sign up for a truck to come by
and they can put their goods on the truck and get dollars or whatever. Easy.

this rewards large farmers, who can be guaranteed to always have a buyer, so
long as they respect the will of supply and demand, and adjust year-on-year.

this rewards distributors, who suddenly have been nationalized and can receive
government dollars while mostly doing the same thing they've been doing.

this rewards the people, who can eat for free.

this rewards the grocery stores, who can compete on things more human than price

this rewards the restaurants, who can always stay busy.

overall I think it's a good idea and a reasonable implementation path. It would
help a lot of people, and change our world for the better.
